#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:4
msgid ""
"Front door for cross-repo peering operations. Picks the right interaction"
" mode (advisory, spec-out, handoff, list, show) from the user's intent "
"and runs the appropriate CLI command with the trail-discipline flags "
"filled in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:9
msgid ""
"Before doing anything, **load `skills/cross-repo-peering/SKILL.md`** — "
"the skill carries the decision tree, the prompt-composition rules, and "
"the anti-patterns. Don't try to compose a peer call without it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:13
msgid "**Steps:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:15
msgid ""
"Run `hero peer list` first to confirm peers are registered. If empty, "
"tell the user to register first with `hero admin repos add <alias> "
"<path>` and stop. Don't try to invoke a peer call against an unregistered"
" alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:20
msgid "Parse the user's intent into one of five sub-actions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "Intent signal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "Sub-action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "\"ask <peer>\", \"check with <peer>\", \"what's <peer>'s X\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "advisory peer call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "\"have <peer> design\", \"let <peer> handle the design of\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "spec-out peer call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "\"hand off to <peer>\", \"drop on <peer>'s queue\", \"transfer to <peer>\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "async handoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "\"pick up\", \"accept\", \"peer finished\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "handoff accept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid ""
"\"list peers\", \"what peers\", \"show <peer>\", \"what does <peer> "
"expose\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md
msgid "discovery (list / show)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:30
msgid ""
"If two sub-actions are plausible (common between advisory and spec-out; "
"common between handoff and spec-out), ask one focused clarifying "
"question. Don't guess."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:34
msgid "**For advisory peer calls** (`--mode=advisory`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:36
msgid ""
"Identify the active spec from the session context. If there is one, "
"attach it: `--related-spec <slug>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:38
msgid ""
"Draft a `--reason` string from the session context (one sentence, why "
"this call is happening now). Show it to the user inline before "
"dispatching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:41
msgid ""
"**Compose the peer-call prompt as a focused brief**, not a paraphrase. "
"Name the specific artifact, field, or constraint. Read the skill's "
"\"Composing a good peer-call prompt\" section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:44
msgid ""
"Default budgets (20 turns / 50,000 tokens) are usually fine; only "
"override if the user asks or the prompt is genuinely huge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:47
msgid "Example output to the user before dispatching:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:49
msgid ""
"Calling `hero-cloud` (advisory mode). Reason: \"Need to know the error "
"envelope shape before changing the renderer in this session.\" Prompt: "
"\"What's the current shape of the `errors` array in the `/v1/order` POST "
"response? Any deprecations in flight?\" Related spec: `order-failure-"
"error-display`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:55
msgid "Run this? [y/n]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:57
msgid "**For spec-out peer calls** (`--mode=spec-out`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:59
msgid "Same trail discipline (`--related-spec`, `--reason`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:60
msgid ""
"**Shape the prompt as a `/design` kickoff** — name the work, list "
"constraints, list out-of-scope, list acceptance shape. The peer's "
"`/design` flow runs on this verbatim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:63
msgid ""
"Default budget is larger (50 turns / 150,000 tokens). Don't override "
"unless the spec is genuinely heavyweight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:65
msgid ""
"Confirm with the user before dispatching — spec-out writes a spec on the "
"peer's side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:68
msgid "**For async handoff**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:70
msgid ""
"Pre-condition: there must be a local spec to hand off. If the user hasn't"
" named one and the session has an active spec, suggest that one. If "
"neither, ask which spec to hand off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:73
msgid ""
"The handoff scaffolds a spec on the peer's side based on the local spec's"
" frontmatter + body. The receiver's title and type can be overridden with"
" `--title` / `--type` if the peer's conventions want a different shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:77
msgid ""
"Run: `hero handoff <local-slug> <peer-alias> --reason \"<why>\" --type "
"<type>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:78
msgid "After the handoff returns, surface to the user:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:79
msgid ""
"The receiver-side slug (may differ from local if there was a collision — "
"Hero appends `-2`, `-3`, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:81
msgid "The trail entry was written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:82
msgid "The local spec's status moved to `handed_off`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:83
msgid "The peer's side now owns the next move."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:85
msgid "**For handoff accept** (when a `handed_back` spec needs picking up):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:87
msgid "Run `hero handoff accept <slug>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:88
msgid ""
"Prompt the user to pick the next status (usually verify the symptom on "
"the originator's side, then mark complete)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:91
msgid "**For discovery** (list / show):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:93
msgid "`hero peer list` for the table view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:94
msgid ""
"`hero peer show <alias>` for one peer's manifest contents and in-flight "
"handoffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:96
msgid "These are read-only; no confirmation needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:98
msgid "**Always surface the result to the user**, not the raw command output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:100
msgid ""
"For advisory: summarize the findings (headline + 2-3 actionable bullets)."
" Quote excerpts; don't dump the full peer envelope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:102
msgid ""
"For spec-out: confirm the peer-side slug was created and that the local "
"spec moved to `awaiting_peer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:104
msgid "For handoff: confirm the peer-side slug and the trail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:105
msgid "For list/show: render the table or detail block plainly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:107
msgid "**Trail discipline checks** — before reporting \"done\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:109
msgid "Did `hero handoff status` show the new entry?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:110
msgid "Is the active spec's frontmatter updated (`status:`, trail block)?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:111
msgid ""
"Did the peer's events log get the corresponding event? (You can check "
"`cat ../<peer-alias>/.hero/events.log | tail -5` if curious.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:114
msgid ""
"**Common patterns** (these should fire from natural language, not just "
"slash invocation):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:117
msgid "\"Ask hero-cloud about X\" → advisory call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:118
msgid "\"Have hero-code design the migration story\" → spec-out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:119
msgid "\"Hand off the tracker-fronting spec to hero-cloud\" → async handoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:120
msgid "\"What peers do we have\" → list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:121
msgid "\"What does hero-cloud expose\" → show"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:123
msgid "**What NOT to do:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:125
msgid ""
"Don't invoke a peer call to answer a question you can answer locally "
"(`hero search`, reading the workspace, etc.). Peer calls cost a subagent "
"spawn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:128
msgid ""
"Don't paraphrase the user's words verbatim as the peer-call prompt. "
"Compose a structured brief."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:130
msgid "Don't skip `--related-spec` when one exists in session context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:131
msgid ""
"Don't run `--mode=full` — full-delivery peer call is v2+; not available "
"in v1. If the user asks, explain and offer spec-out as the closest "
"available option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/peer.md:135
msgid ""
"**What to say:** \"ask peer\", \"ask hero-code about\", \"check with "
"sibling\", \"have hero-cloud design\", \"hand off to\", \"drop on peer's "
"queue\", \"transfer to\", \"list peers\", \"what peers do we have\", "
"\"what does peer expose\", \"pick up the handoff\"."
msgstr ""

